# This file is generated by dune, edit dune-project instead
opam-version: "2.0"
synopsis: "Secp256k1 signing and address derivation for Cosmos SDK chains"
description: """
Signs the 32-byte SHA-256 digest of a serialized SignDoc and produces the
64-byte r||s the SDK expects -- no recovery byte, because the public key
travels in SignerInfo.

Signatures are normalised to low-S. The SDK rejects high-S as malleable and
mirage-crypto-ec does not normalise, so this is a correctness requirement
rather than a preference.

Curve operations use mirage-crypto-ec's fiat-crypto P256k1 backend and are
constant time. Address derivation is RIPEMD-160 over SHA-256 of the
compressed public key, both from digestif. Ed25519 is verify-only: it is a
validator key type, not an account signing path this library offers.

No RNG: nonces are RFC 6979 deterministic."""
maintainer: ["Gil Bahat <bahat.gil@gmail.com>"]
